From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:39:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: answer adb root on a build that is not debuggable as
 AOSP does

LineageOS's "Add ADB root service changes" made restart_root_service
ask adbroot_service first and test the build only when that call fails.
When the service answers, the stored rooted debugging setting is the
only test, so a build that is not debuggable replied "ADB Root access is
disabled by system setting - enable in Settings -> System -> Developer
options". There is no such switch there: the service reports itself
unsupported, and Settings shows none.

Test the build first. A build that is neither ANDROID_DEBUGGABLE nor
ro.debuggable answers "adbd cannot run as root in production builds",
as AOSP does, before adbroot_service is looked up and whatever it would
say. A debuggable build is unchanged: it asks the service and keeps
LineageOS's message for a switch that is off.
---
 daemon/restart_service.cpp | 18 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/daemon/restart_service.cpp b/daemon/restart_service.cpp
index d6d4b2446c55dac666293a5bb752cc7b01782564..2dca6e6ba892ee16a8e7c38b952560f60ea3143a 100644
--- a/daemon/restart_service.cpp
+++ b/daemon/restart_service.cpp
@@ -39,6 +39,14 @@ void restart_root_service(unique_fd fd) {
         return;
     }
 
+    // A build that is not debuggable never runs adbd as root. Answer as AOSP does, before
+    // adbroot_service is asked and whatever it would say: its rooted debugging setting has no
+    // switch on such a build.
+    if (!ANDROID_DEBUGGABLE && !__android_log_is_debuggable()) {
+        WriteFdExactly(fd.get(), "adbd cannot run as root in production builds\n");
+        return;
+    }
+
 #if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(__ANDROID_RECOVERY__)
     ndk::SpAIBinder binder = ndk::SpAIBinder(AServiceManager_getService("adbroot_service"));
     std::shared_ptr<aidl::android::adbroot::IAdbRootService> service =
@@ -51,15 +59,7 @@ void restart_root_service(unique_fd fd) {
 
 #if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(__ANDROID_RECOVERY__)
     bool enabled = false;
-    if (auto status = service->getEnabled(&enabled); !status.isOk()) {
-#endif
-    if (!ANDROID_DEBUGGABLE && !__android_log_is_debuggable()) {
-        WriteFdExactly(fd.get(), "adbd cannot run as root in production builds\n");
-        return;
-    }
-#if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(__ANDROID_RECOVERY__)
-    }
-    if (!enabled) {
+    if (!service->getEnabled(&enabled).isOk() || !enabled) {
         WriteFdExactly(fd, "ADB Root access is disabled by system setting - "
                 "enable in Settings -> System -> Developer options\n");
         return;
